From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:26:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/30] =?UTF-8?q?Tokens:=20"for=20each=20opponent,=20creat?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20=E2=80=A6=20attacking=20that=20player"=20attacks=20each?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adeline, Resplendent Cathar: "Whenever you attack, for each opponent,
create a 1/1 white Human creature token that's tapped and attacking that
player or a planeswalker they control." Ruling: one token for each
opponent, attacking that opponent.

CR 508.4: a creature put onto the battlefield attacking attacks the
player the effect names. CR 608.2c: "that player" is each opponent in
turn. phase folded "for each opponent" into the token count and seated
every token against one derived defender, so all of them attacked the
same player (combat::enter_attacking from token.rs).

- Parser (assembly.rs): a repeated attacking-token clause whose text
  names the attacked player ("attacking that player/opponent") iterates
  the players (player_scope) instead of folding them into the count; the
  token's owner is the controller from before the iteration
  (OriginalController).
- TokenSpec gains entry_attack_player (serde default None): the player an
  attacking token enters attacking. It is set when the token is made for
  an opponent of its creator during a per-player iteration, and the
  creation loop seats such a token against that player.

Not done: the controller can't choose one of that player's planeswalkers
instead; the token attacks the player.

Mechanical: entry_attack_player: None in every TokenSpec literal.

Card data: the parse change reaches games only with card data generated
by this parser; Yama's pinned card data has the old count.

Test: issue_3303_adeline_tapped_attacking.rs,
adeline_makes_one_attacking_human_for_each_opponent (three players).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
